  "The ad load measurably worsened in the second half of 2024 and has only partially recovered — ad-complaint share by half-year 2021H2 3.5% → 2022H1 11.9% → 2022H2 7.4% → 2023H1 11.8% → 2023H2 13.2% → 2024H1 22.0% → 2024H2 39.6% → 2025H1 34.4% → 2025H2 32.6% → 2026H1 18.8% → 2026H2 16.7%; the corpus mean tracks it 4.729 (2021) → 4.180 → 3.877 → 3.810 (2024) → 3.846 → 4.048 (2026); users noticed and said so — 'Since then, the amount of ads has increased HEAVILY' (14 months of use); 'The developers got too greedy I guess'; 'Seems like every update just brings more paywall and more forced advertisements'; 'I wish they would go back to like 1 or 2 ads max'; 2024H2 is the inflection point and the 2026 improvement is real but leaves the rate ~5× the 2021 baseline",
  "ad frequency raised in 2024H2", "churn", "3.5% → 39.6% → 16.7%; mean 4.729 → 3.810 → 4.048", "dont", "high confidence", "yes",
